1. Qb8+ {The queen gives check, at the adverse queen's knight's square.} Ke7 {The king, at his
second square.} 2. Qg8 {The queen, at the adverse king's knight's square.} Rc6 {The rook, at its
queen's bishop's third square.} 3. Ke5 {The king, at the adverse king's fourth square.} Re6+
{The rook, at its king's third square, giving check.} 4. Kd5 {The king, at the adverse queen's
fourth square. (a) NOTE: In this position, it is a drawn-game, because the queen cannot take
backwards, neither the king nor the pawn, as in the former party.} *
